WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.800
School Rumble will start soon after this !

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.230
I will make you happy.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.720
Althought it might make me look insensitive for saying such a thing right now.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.890
I still must say it!

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:20.410
Come with me!

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.920
Tsu...ka...Tsukamoto has been kidnapped!

00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:13.660
Harima-kun, where are we going?

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.140
You are making me feel uneasy.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.100
Don't talk or you'll bite your tongue!

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.280
We are going to the airport!

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.160
What's going on?

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:24.950
Don't tell me we are going to see Karasuma-kun?

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.410
No! I don't want to go!

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.790
Why? You want me and Karasuma-kun to meet?

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.140
Is it for my sake?

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.960
It's okay already!

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.820
Hey, are you listening, Harima-kun?

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.170
Stop! Stop!

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:40.880
Hey! Don't jut do whatever you want!

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.010
What exactly are you thinking of?

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.470
Please! Let me down!

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.860
Stop doing such meaningless things!

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.700
Harima-san, threw his feelings aside once again.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.660
Towards the airport?

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:05.620
It seems so.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.110
In order to let Nee-san and Karasuma-senpai to meet.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.080
I expected this to happen if it's that idiot.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.920
Stop already. Harima-senpai is taking a gamble...

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.520
I say, Yakumo.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.760
Do you think that Hige has thought this out?

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:24.090
That fellow must be thinking this is as easy as boarding a train in the city.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:28.310
Do you think Harima-kun will buy such a ticket without preparing beforehand?

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:32.270
Even if there is the determination, he will only be at a loss when he reaches the airport.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.690
Excuse me!

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:39.710
Say, American-bound flights are through Haneda?

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.690
Or through Narita?

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.770
It should be Narita, I suppose. If you're talking about international flights.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:44.720
Thanks!

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.660
Save me! Kidnap!

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.130
She's my little sister!

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.810
Dammit. What do I do when I get there?

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.270
A ticket to America is about 20 thousand yen right?

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.000
That much should be sufficient!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.990
And speaking of which, why am I doing such a thing?

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.800
That motorcycle with the two people, stop now!

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.930
Move to the side and stop!

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:06.170
Shit! I'm busy right now!

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.950
Oi! Stop now!

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:18.060
Stop immediately! That motorcycle with the two of you!

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.040
So this is it?

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.590
Hahahaha! Japanese police are outstanding aren't they?

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.040
W-what's going on?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.650
But that's as far as you go!

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.830
Togo Masakazu... has arrived!

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.450
W-what are you doing?

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.260
Get down! It's dangerous!

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.490
We can't just stop just like that.

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:43.920
You can't stop this bike... or love.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.050
Yo! Why do you have that look on your face?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.320
To truth is.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:53.340
Is there any need to explain? A hero will always sense the dangers around his allies.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:55.050
Although we want to say that,

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.510
Akira called actually.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.720
And told us to give you a hand.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.940
It's Eri still trying to prepare a ticket.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.740
Mikoto and Yakumo are helping to prepare for the journey too.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.840
Akira and them? Why?

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:09.860
Who knows?

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:10.940
Hey!

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.130
Say, it looks we don't have much time for talk. Let's do it!

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:17.460
OK.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.400
Adios!

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.200
Hey, it's dangerous!

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.630
Danger is part of being a man.

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:23.590
Sorry about that.

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:26.900
Why did Eri and them even...

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:28.980
I have already...

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:30.010
Tsukamoto!

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.530
You better not let go of me!

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.170
Miyanogi should be in this direction!

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:48.990
The gas?! There is still some. Thanks to Itoko !

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.470
Even I can't look at the meter.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:54.410
It should be enough to reach there! I'm counting on you!

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.330
I will protect her!

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.320
It's really weird.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.320
About me. A person like me.

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.590
If the me from past was to see this, what would he say?

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.210
He will definitely say this.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:16.920
You're really an idiot! Just let go! If not won't you just get weaker and weaker?

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.730
This sort of thing doesn't suit you!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.250
This is really sickening! Just stop already!

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:25.330
He might probably say such a thing, Harima Kenji.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.860
Why are you doing such a thing?

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.530
Because you are in love!

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.400
Towards this person, I have love and love until I can't help it!

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:36.070
Enough! That reason is good enough!

00:06:36.070 --> 00:06:37.860
I can run forward for that!

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:39.810
What are you saying, Harima-kun?

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.090
Ah! Nothing! I have to do it!

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:49.760
Right. Just like this. I'm now about to drink.

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.810
Mm? And I'm going to sleep right after this.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.810
Then I'll drink while I wait for you.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.220
Itoko. Sorry but I need to borrow the motorbike.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.550
Don't ask for the reason.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.170
That Kenji...

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.120
It's really easy for people to change.

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:21.900
Look!

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.170
Go! Don't slow down!

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.560
Hime-ojou should have already sent the mail about the location to you.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:39.600
Harima-kun, umm...

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.810
Go!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:48.710
Fourth floor. Internation flights departure counter.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.390
Flight number GAL408.

00:07:50.390 --> 00:07:51.810
G counter.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.980
I have to find it here?!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:02.040
G... G... G...

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:06.570
Excuse me, where is the counter for flight GAL 408 bound for New York?

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.000
Would you like to check in?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.380
Eh? Passport?

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.890
It's all over!

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:18.890
Miss!

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.590
In short she will go on the next flight.

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:29.060
For the time being, Hige just find something to do.

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:31.040
It can't be!

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:41.450
Youko will be rushing over to bring your passport, luggage and some living expenses.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:42.530
Youko?

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:44.870
Ah...I mean Sasakura-sensei.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:45.980
Here's some coffee.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:50.040
She's Itoko...I mean Osakabe-sensei's friend.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:50.920
She was so from a very long time.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:56.420
I see. You are living with Osakabe-sensei, aren't you?

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.260
The feeling must be somewhat different.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:00.410
I guess.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.860
In my eyes it's just like living with a big sister.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:04.290
I still feel that it's rather normal.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.680
Don't you like her?

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:07.580
No way?!

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:11.410
I'm not interrested in old sister type women!

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:15.930
ohh? I guess you are used to pretty girls with good style.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.760
No wonder you are not charmed by normal girls.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:21.030
That's why girls like Eri-chan and Yakumo...

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:23.550
What do you mean by normal?

00:09:23.550 --> 00:09:27.500
But, I have my own opinion beauty too.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:30.610
Actually I do go for girls like Ojou. Not at all.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.420
Eh? Why? Isn't she cute?

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:36.970
She tries to behave cool though she doesn't know everything.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:40.300
Then what kind of girl do you like?

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:43.340
That...right...

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:47.080
A little dumb. Slow. Daydreamer. Not calculative.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.770
And talks loudly. That's the kind of woman.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.710
You like that kind?! You're weird!

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:55.740
No matter from what angle I see, you fit all those categories!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:58.470
Realise a litte, idiot woman!

00:10:01.190 --> 00:10:04.070
Never mind. It's not like it matters.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:06.050
Hey, Harima-kun.

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:06.660
What is it?

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:12.380
Harima-kun, why do you think that I should go see Karasuma-kun?

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:16.260
Nothing really. It's my feeling.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.060
Feeling?

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:21.330
Listen well. Although I don't know what he said,

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:24.890
it's a lie and definitely not something from the bottom of his heart.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.890
Furthermore,

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:26.970
Furthermore?

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.300
There will be a day for you when...

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.560
a guy who likes you will appear.

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.910
If it's like that, that person will be miserable.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:36.480
Why?

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:41.200
Because, of the man's intention.

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:46.550
He will try to snatch you away from Karasuma,

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.250
Remember that for the rest of your life.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:56.170
I...see...

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:59.390
What's wrong? You are suddenly so serious.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:01.020
Nothing.

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:03.290
Speaking of which, Harima-kun's sunglasses...

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.180
Could it be for the sake of hiding your identity from me?

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:10.420
I knew it! I have seen you somewhere before!

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.650
Right? Right? Right?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.360
No! I have never seen you before!

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.610
Liar! It must be that time...

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.110
Wait! Wait! Itoko's calling.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:23.370
The luggage's here. That's fast~!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.070
Hey, that's cunning!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.490
Thank you very much!

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:31.190
It's alright.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.510
We are teachers for the moment anyway.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:37.000
We've got to help sometimes too.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.790
If you don't hurry, you won't be able to make in time to the departure gate.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:41.940
Take care!

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.970
Kenji, go see her off.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.710
Sheesh, you're so noisy.

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.930
Passengers boarding flight number GAL408,

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.890
Please move to the departure gate for international flights on the fourth floor.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.290
Here, let's hurry!

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.230
Goodbye, Tenma-chan.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.780
This is our true goodbye now.

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:07.050
I can give you my blessings on walking your own path while sending you off.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.100
I'm feeling happy now.

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:10.230
Thank you.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.710
I was really glad to be in the same class as you.

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:18.170
The departure gates. So it's here?

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.310
What's wrong, Tsukamoto?

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.130
Nothing.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.530
I'm really glad that I was in this class.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.030
Me too.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.600
Let's meet again, ok?

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:44.760
25 March, Tsukamoto went to America.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:50.150
It was immediately spring. The season that suited her best.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:56.460
You know...when Harima-kun was shouting to himself on the motorbike...

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.080
I heard it.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:02.580
No, actually...

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:05.640
It was earlier, perhaps...

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:12.450
Goodbye. Your feelings made me feel very proud.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.720
Thank you, Harima-kun.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.910
It has been a day since Nee-san left.

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:38.070
It's much faster with just one person.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:41.290
Iori?

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:46.010
Hmm...Nee-san?

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:50.150
Nee-san...won't be coming back for the time being.

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:51.860
Lonely?

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:56.140
But...let's support her.

00:14:01.430 --> 00:14:04.150
How is it? The feeling of living alone?

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.860
Mm, it has been okay so far.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:10.720
I'm glad. Let us come here to liven up the place.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:14.070
Yo.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.580
Sorry to disturb!

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.170
Cheese!

00:14:17.170 --> 00:14:18.540
Sorry to disturb!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.010
Yo. Sorry for comning late.

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:22.500
Sorry!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.460
Today is the celebration for the walking festival.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:41.090
But...Harima-san...

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.190
Really? That kind of thing...

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.760
Don't blow your smoke in the face of others, bastard.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.090
Hang on!

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:05.940
Hey! Stop there! Do you hear me?

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:30.680
What are you doing here?

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:34.560
Hey! You... are you injured?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.660
I said to leave me alone!

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:44.490
I can't just leave you here looking like that can I?

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:47.950
Really...Not only were you dumped, you went to pick a fight?

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:50.430
It's really hard to believe. A person like can still be considered a man?

00:15:50.430 --> 00:15:52.430
Exactly how much must you fake before you are satisfied?

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:54.950
Shrilling ! Noisy! You idiot woman!

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:58.610
No doubt, this is just a small matter to you.

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:00.960
This is where I can see that you are most unhappy about.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:04.580
A woman like you who keeps changing your men.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:07.830
I'll never want to have relations with you. It's disgusting!

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:08.900
What did you say...

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:13.860
You're such a loose woman! What a kind of person you are? Playing with peoples feelings all the time.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:16.370
Who would like such a woman?

00:16:16.940 --> 00:16:20.990
A cheap girl like you doesn't have any feelings huh?

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:22.430
Is that so?

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:23.830
Ouch!

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:25.790
It hurts! You...!

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.220
Why are you crying?

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:34.510
I'm not crying.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.250
Don't lie! You obviously...

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.180
I said I'm not crying!

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:39.600
You...!!

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.840
You really piss me off!

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.650
What right do you have to say that about of me?

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:47.860
Have you ever understood me completely? It's so arrogant of you!

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:52.430
I'm just like you, to date once is just enough. Do you understand?

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:55.120
Men! To just find one is enough!

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:57.180
But that is rather difficult.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:00.370
Being cute will also have the troubles of being cute too.

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:03.360
Nobody can really understand the inner me.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.920
Men are all the same. They are all idiots...idiots.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:15.260
I hate it...I hate all men! I hate them to the core!

00:17:16.100 --> 00:17:18.300
It's alright if I don't date for the rest of my life.

00:17:21.550 --> 00:17:24.730
How is it that I'm totally loose?

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:30.620
Honestly I have never gone out on a real date with anyone before.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:35.830
Someday there will be a person who will love me from the bottom of his heart...

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:39.950
Although at times I will hate my own young, foolish feelings,

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:45.720
no matter who I go out with, it doesn't feel right.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.600
You...

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:56.320
Forget it! Forget it! Forget it! Forget it!

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.740
Exactly how did you...?!

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.180
W-what's with you...??

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.270
Nothing. This is really effective.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:12.620
I have woken up. Thanks, Ojou.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.650
Thanks, Ojou.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:25.370
Not long after Harima-senpai disappeared.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.850
Not telling where he went, he threw away his cellphone too.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.750
Meanwhile, the girl in America...

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:36.950
Karasuma-kun!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.250
Karasuma-kun's illness?

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:46.140
It seems his illness isn't life-threatening.

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.600
What! That means he can still be with Tsukamoto...

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:53.060
I say that but...

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:58.030
Karasuma seems to have lost his ability to think.

00:18:58.690 --> 00:19:01.990
So what we really was saying was,

00:19:02.370 --> 00:19:06.400
Even if they were together, it would be a love that he could not recognise for a life time,

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:07.950
A love that cannot be reciprocated.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:12.060
He cannot let Tenma be bound by this.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:16.090
A love that cannot be loved.

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.880
Do you think something like that could be endured?

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:27.480
But Nee-san did not give up.

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:44.380
Nee-san will never...

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:53.790
Days pass by one by one.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:58.920
From other people, we heard that Harima-san was wandering in another country.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:07.580
Nee-san!

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:09.960
Dear Yakumo-sama,

00:20:10.660 --> 00:20:14.070
Many important things happened yesterday.

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:16.730
I can't stop crying.

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:22.200
Karasuma-kun...remembered something of the past.

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.390
Karasum-senpai...

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:29.240
After talking to Tanizaki-sensei, it seems he told this to Hanai-kun too.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:32.370
Hanai-kun said he tried to call together all of class 2-C.

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:36.330
Surely, all his memories will definitely be recovered.

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:39.110
Right, Yakumo?

00:20:54.970 --> 00:20:57.060
Hey, Ichijou! It's been some time!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.860
We saw "Dojiboron Has Returned!" not long ago.

00:20:59.860 --> 00:21:02.180
It was full of action.

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:03.530
Thank you!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:04.600
D.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:05.990
What?

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.950
No! It's E...it's E!!

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:12.370
Imadori! The sun's wrath!

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:14.480
An indecent fellow!

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:16.760
Kyosuke.

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:18.830
Nothing has changed in those bunch of people there.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:22.130
Hahahaha..this is just right.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:27.260
A man's soul will never change forever, partner.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.850
I'm not your partner.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.510
Great! Everyone's...

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.350
With this memorable setting,

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:35.960
We will help our main character regain his memories today!

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:41.810
Regarding this, I, Hanai Haruki, have a suggestion!

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:45.880
In order to let him remember the friendship bonds we had in class, let's sing a song!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.200
Pie fight!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.610
What!?

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:54.070
I didn't hear about this!

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:57.540
Eh...if you want to play it like this...

00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.000
It's not my fault...!

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.630
Enough talk!

00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:15.150
Isn't it memorable, Karasuma-kun?

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:20.750
He's spaced out. There's still times when he's just spaced out?

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:27.320
Thank you!

00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:48.710
The activity you're doing is rather interesting. As usual.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:52.790
I didn't get the notice about the class reunion.

00:22:52.790 --> 00:22:55.520
Some classmates you are.

00:23:00.660 --> 00:23:03.860
Ah...you are...Ha...

00:23:04.050 --> 00:23:06.820
Eh? His memory returned?

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:07.900
Karasuma-kun!

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:11.430
Ha...Hanai-kun.

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:13.490
Disappointing~!

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:19.910
Tsukamoto, I ended up coming here.

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:22.880
Sorry.

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:25.090
Harima-kun.

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:32.800
Tsukamoto, I...I...I...

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:38.960
W-what's with you, Tsukamoto?

00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:44.290
Why did you make others cry, you bastard?

00:23:44.290 --> 00:23:46.900
I was originally going to think of saying long time no see.

00:23:46.710 --> 00:23:49.860
No! It's a misunderstanding! A misunderstanding!

00:23:50.250 --> 00:23:53.040
Enough! Get him!

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:03.880
Welcome back, Harima-kun!
